---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

// The three stones at the mouth of the channel link to the real text once
// it is published; until then each one points at its forthcoming entry.
const all = await getCollection('essays');
const byNumber = (n: string) => all.find((e) => e.data.number === n);
const a0 = byNumber('A0');
const e1 = byNumber('01');
const e2 = byNumber('02');
const hrefFor = (e: typeof a0, fallback: string) =>
  e ? (e.data.kind === 'register' ? '/assumptions' : `/${e.id}`) : fallback;
---
<Base surface="landing" description="The centre is not a compromise. It is where the flow steadies. Essays from the quiet part of the river.">
  <Fragment slot="under">
    <canvas id="river" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="hero" id="top">
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 16%; left: 7%; font-size: 19px; --wd: 26s; --wl: -4s; --wx: 60px; --wy: -24px; --wr: -6deg; --wo: 0.4;">prawda</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 30%; left: 13%; font-size: 15px; --wd: 34s; --wl: -12s; --wx: 44px; --wy: 30px; --wr: 4deg; --wo: 0.3;">veritas</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 58%; left: 6%; font-size: 17px; --wd: 30s; --wl: -8s; --wx: 52px; --wy: -36px; --wr: -3deg; --wo: 0.35;">αλήθεια</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 74%; left: 15%; font-size: 14px; --wd: 38s; --wl: -20s; --wx: 36px; --wy: 22px; --wr: 5deg; --wo: 0.28;">vérité</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 18%; right: 8%; font-size: 17px; --wd: 32s; --wl: -6s; --wx: -56px; --wy: 26px; --wr: 5deg; --wo: 0.38;">真理</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 36%; right: 14%; font-size: 15px; --wd: 28s; --wl: -16s; --wx: -40px; --wy: -30px; --wr: -4deg; --wo: 0.3;">satya</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 60%; right: 7%; font-size: 19px; --wd: 36s; --wl: -10s; --wx: -60px; --wy: 20px; --wr: 3deg; --wo: 0.4;">wahrheit</span>
    <span class="driftword" style="top: 78%; right: 13%; font-size: 14px; --wd: 31s; --wl: -22s; --wx: -38px; --wy: -26px; --wr: -5deg; --wo: 0.28;">truth</span>

    <div class="kicker">essays from the quiet part of the river</div>
    <h1 class="settle" id="headline"><span class="ln">The centre is not a compromise.</span><span class="ln">It is where the flow <em>steadies</em>.</span></h1>
    <p class="sub">Ideas arrive turbulent, from every bank and in every tongue. The work of the middle is laminar: assumptions stated, opposition steelmanned, statistics read honestly &mdash; until the current runs clear enough to drink from.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="cta" href="#gate">Enter the stream</a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href={hrefFor(a0, '/assumptions')}>read the assumptions first &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    <div class="scrollcue">the currents meet in the middle &darr;</div>
  </section>

  <section class="band confluence reveal">
    <div class="band-inner">
      <p>Both currents carry something true, and both arrive shouting. This is the place where they are made to <em>speak in turn</em>.</p>
      <div class="attrib">the house rule</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band gate" id="gate">
    <div class="band-inner">
      <div class="gate-head reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow">the foundations &middot; read in order</div>
        <h2>Three stones stand at the mouth of the channel.</h2>
        <p>Everything downstream builds on them. If you reject one, you will know exactly where we part &mdash; honestly, and without a fight.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stones">
        <a class="stone reveal" href={hrefFor(a0, '/assumptions')}>
          <span class="num">A0</span>
          <h3>The Assumptions</h3>
          <p>Everything taken as given, stated plainly. A standing register that changes only by explicit, dated ruling &mdash; nothing here shifts quietly.</p>
          <span class="go">{a0 ? 'read the register' : 'forthcoming'} &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="stone reveal" href={hrefFor(e1, '/essays#foundations')}>
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h3>Objective truth, and what force must answer to</h3>
          <p>There is a way things are, and it can referee our disputes. Shared tests let us correct each other; a coercive rule needs checkable facts <em>and</em> a defence of its own.</p>
          <span class="go">{e1 ? 'read the essay' : 'forthcoming'} &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="stone reveal" href={hrefFor(e2, '/essays#foundations')}>
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h3>Statistics: the most important tool, and the most abused</h3>
          <p>Distributions show you a society. They inform, but do not settle, what we may conclude about the person in front of you. Evidence, treatment and publication are three different judgments.</p>
          <span class="go">{e2 ? 'read the essay' : 'forthcoming'} &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band channel-band" id="channel">
    <div class="channel reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">from essay one</div>
      <p>Begin with the sentence most of this site hangs on: <em>there is a way things are.</em> Not a way for you and a way for me &mdash; a way, full stop, indifferent to preference, party, or mood.</p>
      <p>Now watch what the sentence does. Two people disagree about something that matters &mdash; a dosage, a bridge load, whether the well water is safe. If there is a way things are, their disagreement has a referee. Not a person: a direction. They can be wrong. They can find out.</p>
      <p class="pull">Nobody submits to a person; both submit to the way things are.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band stillness reveal" id="still">
    <div class="band-inner">
      <div class="waterline" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <svg class="keystone-svg" width="120" height="78" viewBox="0 0 48 30" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 28 A20 20 0 0 1 44 28 L37 28 A13 13 0 0 0 11 28 Z" fill="#1B222B" stroke="#56606C" stroke-width="0.8"></path>
        <polygon class="key" points="19.2,8.6 28.8,8.6 26.6,15.4 21.4,15.4" fill="#D9A441" stroke="#0E141A" stroke-width="1.2"></polygon>
      </svg>
      <h2>When the water is still, you can see the bottom.</h2>
      <p class="commit">I start from one thing: there is a way things are, independent of what anyone prefers. You need not grant it to come further. If you will share the practical work &mdash; checking claims, correcting mistakes, keeping rules open to challenge &mdash; that is already common ground.</p>
      <a class="cta" href={hrefFor(e1, '/essays#foundations')}>{e1 ? 'Begin with Essay I' : 'See what is coming'}</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline src="/landing.js"></script>
</Base>
